>-- 
One possibility is that your new computer is too fast to run the
games. Many older games try to determine the speed of your computer
with a simple timing loop, that was designed to cope with the
fastest PC chips available at the time the game was written. Anything
faster such as a 486, or worse a pentium, will cause an internal
counter to overflow and make wondrous things happen.

You could try using SLOWITDOWN or a similar utility designed to
deliberately waste most of your computer's power.
